<spell-notebook "placeholder usage">
	<header level="1">
		Placeholder
		<header>A placeholder is used to reserve space for content that soon will appear in a layout.</>
	</>
	<placeholder-tab-bar showing="usage"/>
	<section>
		<html>
			<ui-menu class="ui-docs-section-tabs" appearance="segmented" aria-label="Sections">
				<ui-item link="#using-it">Using it</>
				<ui-item link="#keyboard">Keyboard</>
				<ui-item link="#accessibility">Accessibility</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<!-- USAGE:  building a skeleton, swapping it for content, accessibility. -->
	<section label="Using it">
		<markdown>
			Build a skeleton from four shapes inside a `<ui-placeholder>`:

			- `<ui-placeholder-header>`: two taller bars, with an optional square `image` beside them
			- `<ui-placeholder-paragraph>`: a group of lines
			- `<ui-placeholder-line>`: one bar; `length` fixes its length, else it varies by its position
			- `<ui-placeholder-image>`: a block of fixed height, or `square` (1:1) / `rectangular` (4:3) at its container's
			  width

			The shapes must sit inside a `<ui-placeholder>`: that is where their look comes from. A shimmer sweeps across every
			shape on the page in step; it stops when the reader prefers reduced motion.

			A placeholder has no events and no "loaded" state: replace it with the real content when that arrives.
		</>
		<markdown>
			```html
			<section aria-busy="true">
			  <ui-placeholder>
			    <ui-placeholder-paragraph>
			      <ui-placeholder-line></ui-placeholder-line>
			      <ui-placeholder-line></ui-placeholder-line>
			    </ui-placeholder-paragraph>
			  </ui-placeholder>
			</section>
			<!-- when the data is in:  swap the placeholder for the content, then remove aria-busy -->
			```
		</>
		<markdown>
			Every tag that has a `skeleton` in its vocabulary gets one from `<ui-root>` while its family loads: the same shapes,
			built for you.
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Keyboard">
		<markdown>None: a placeholder takes no focus and holds nothing to reach.</>
	</>

	<section label="Accessibility">
		<markdown>
			- A placeholder is decorative: it is hidden from screen readers and holds no text.
			- Announce the loading once, on the region that is loading: `aria-busy="true"` on it, a
			  [loader](/components/ui/ui-loader.html), or a [segment](/components/ui/ui-segment.html) with `loading`.
			- The shimmer stops for readers who prefer reduced motion; the shapes stay as a flat tint.
			- If the placeholder fails to render, it shows its shapes through a bare `<slot>`, without the
			  placeholder's own box and look.
		</>
	</>
</spell-notebook>
